     "A new computer led to me having to re-install software.   <div><br></div><div>Unfortunately, something seems to have changed in R since I last used the package.</div><div><br></div><div>When I opened R, I received the following warning:</div><div><br></div><div>Warning: namespace ‘lavaan’ is not available and has been replaced<br>by .GlobalEnv when processing object ‘Results1.1’<br>[Previously saved workspace restored]<br><br></div><div><br></div><div>I don&#39;t know what this means, and I installed Lavaan using:</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(71,88,171);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">install.packages</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">(</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(32,121,77);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">&quot;lavaan&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">, </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(101,116,34);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">dependencies =</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"> </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(143,89,2);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">)</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\">I received the following confirmation:</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,59,79);font-family:SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,&quot;Courier New&quot;,monospace;font-size:14.875px;white-space:pre;background-color:rgba(233,236,239,0.65)\"><br></span></div><div>package ‘lavaan’ successfully unpacked and MD5 sums checked<br></div><div><br></div><div>When I verified the install with library(lavaan), I received the following error:</div><div><br></div>Error: package or namespace load failed for ‘lavaan’ in loadNamespace(j &lt;- i[[1L]], c(lib.loc, .libPaths()), versionCheck = vI[[j]]):<br> there is no package called ‘pbivnorm’<div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Bottom line: I can&#39;t run any lavaan syntax.<br><br>Can anyone help?  I can&#39;t seem to find anything online to debug this issue.</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,<br><div> </div></div>"
